# JRebirth AF — snapshot and release versions

Framework-only skill. Covers the **JRebirth** repository (`org.jrebirth.af/`), not application consumers.

## Hard rules

1. **Never publish to Maven Central** (tag `jrebirth-*` or `workflow_dispatch` release) unless the maintainer **explicitly approves** that release version.
2. While waiting for approval, keep `12.x-dev` on **`-SNAPSHOT`** (e.g. `12.0.1-SNAPSHOT`).
3. Before any tooling release, **`PluginDescriptorGoalsTest` must pass** (`text2fx` and `ecore2fx` in `plugin.xml`, no empty `<mojos/>`).
4. **Maven Central 12.0.0 `jrebirth-maven-plugin` is broken** — republish under **12.0.1+** only; do not reuse 12.0.0 coordinates.

## Version layout

| Branch | POM version | Where artifacts go |
|--------|-------------|-------------------|
| `12.x-dev` | `X.Y.Z-SNAPSHOT` | GitHub Packages (`-Pgithub-packages`, workflow `snapshot.yml`) |
| Tag `jrebirth-X.Y.Z` | `X.Y.Z` (CI `versions:set`) | Maven Central (`-Pdeploy-central`, workflow `release-maven-central.yml`) |

Parent: `org.jrebirth:organization:6.0.0` (Organization-POM on Central).

## Bump dev version (local)

PowerShell (quote the version — dots break unquoted `-D` args):

```powershell
mvn -f org.jrebirth.af/pom.xml -B "org.codehaus.mojo:versions-maven-plugin:2.18.0:set" "-DnewVersion=12.0.1-SNAPSHOT" -DprocessAllModules=true -DgenerateBackupPoms=false
```

Helper:

```powershell
powershell -File org.jrebirth.af/.cursor/skills/release-version/scripts/bump-af-version.ps1 -NewVersion 12.0.1-SNAPSHOT
```

After bump: fix orphan POMs outside the reactor if any still reference an old parent version (`form/`, `tooling/genmodel/`, `showcase/data/`).

## Validate tooling (mandatory before release)

```powershell
mvn -f org.jrebirth.af/pom.xml -pl tooling/jrebirth-maven-plugin test
```

Site wiring tests:

```powershell
mvn -f org.jrebirth.af/pom.xml test -pl core -Dtest=AiKitAssemblyDescriptorTest,FrameworkBundleAssemblyDescriptorTest
```

## Site downloads (`pre-site`)

Built into `org.jrebirth.af/target/site/downloads/`:

| File | Assembly |
|------|----------|
| `jrebirth-ai-kit-${project.version}.zip` | `src/assembly/ai-kit.xml` |
| `jrebirth-${project.version}.zip` | `src/assembly/framework-bundle.xml` (library JARs + sources) |

Requires a prior **`mvn install`** so module `target/*.jar` exist before `mvn site`.

Fast site (aggregator only): see `preview-site` skill.

```powershell
mvn -f org.jrebirth.af/pom.xml clean install -Dmaven.test.skip=true
mvn -f org.jrebirth.af/pom.xml site -N -Dmaven.javadoc.skip=true
```

Public site path: `sites/org.jrebirth-${version}/` (hosted as `https://sites.jrebirth.org/org.jrebirth-${version}/`).

## Upload site + showcase apps (IONOS legacy)

```powershell
powershell -File tools/upload-site-and-apps.ps1 -Version 12.0.1
```

`-Version` defaults from `org.jrebirth.af/pom.xml` (SNAPSHOT suffix kept for local artifact names; remote showcase paths use the same version string you pass).

## Release checklist (Central — gated)

**Stop here until the maintainer approves.**

1. All apps that depend on JRebirth are aligned on the release version and build green (local SNAPSHOT or GitHub Packages).
2. `PluginDescriptorGoalsTest` green on the commit to release.
3. Maintainer approves Central publish for `X.Y.Z`.
4. Tag `jrebirth-X.Y.Z` and push, **or** run GitHub Action **Release to Maven Central** with version `X.Y.Z` (no `SNAPSHOT`).
5. Verify Central `org.jrebirth.af.tooling:jrebirth-maven-plugin:X.Y.Z` lists `text2fx` and `ecore2fx`.
6. Build site + upload (`tools/upload-site-and-apps.ps1 -Version X.Y.Z`).
7. On `12.x-dev`, bump to next snapshot (e.g. `12.0.2-SNAPSHOT`) and commit.

Central exclusions (unchanged): `sample`, `distribution`, `showcase/*` — see `README-MAVEN-CENTRAL.md`.

## Related skills

- `preview-site` — local HTML preview
- `update-site-doc` — doc pages and download links when version or assemblies change